Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/mediacodecdec: add Media3's configuration keys and a listener switch as options

On a MediaTek projector (Plezy #2654), 24 fps AV1 through
c2.mtk.av1.decoder stutters under mpv while ExoPlayer plays the same
file smoothly. mpv hands every frame to the codec on time, yet the
display shows about one in seven a refresh late. FFmpeg configures the
decoder differently from Media3's MediaCodecVideoRenderer in three ways
a vendor decoder may time its output by: Media3 sets max-width and
max-height to the stream's size when it plays a single stream, sends the
stream's colour description (color-standard, color-transfer,
color-range), and registers a frame-rendered listener only when
tunneling, where this decoder registers one on every surface.

Add each difference as an option, so a user on such a device can try
them one at a time. The defaults keep the current configuration:

- max_size (0): max-width/max-height at the stream's size.
- color_keys (0): the colour keys with Media3's values (the standard
  from the primaries, SDR transfers as SDR_VIDEO), from the container's
  description where the demuxer passed one, as Media3 does, else from
  the stream's parameter sets (H.264/HEVC SPS VUI, the AV1 sequence
  header).
- rendered_feedback (1): 0 skips the frame-rendered listener, and
  av_mediacodec_rendered_source() answers "off:option".

Each key sent is logged at info level, so a log shows which
configuration a decode ran with.

diff --git a/libavcodec/mediacodec.h b/libavcodec/mediacodec.h
index 34b2b97..f64d59a 100644
--- a/libavcodec/mediacodec.h
+++ b/libavcodec/mediacodec.h
@@ -164,7 +164,8 @@ int av_mediacodec_drain_rendered(AVMediaCodecBuffer *buffer,
  * AMediaCodec_setOnFrameRenderedCallback is, otherwise an "off:" reason —
  * "off:api" (no bridge class on the Java wrapper, or the platform predates
  * the listener: Java API 23, NDK Android 13), "off:codec" (the codec refused
- * the callback), "off:surface" (no output surface).
+ * the callback), "off:surface" (no output surface), "off:option" (the
+ * decoder's rendered_feedback option is off).
  */
 const char *av_mediacodec_rendered_source(const AVMediaCodecBuffer *buffer);
 
diff --git a/libavcodec/mediacodecdec.c b/libavcodec/mediacodecdec.c
index 707a0f5..91f4456 100644
--- a/libavcodec/mediacodecdec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/mediacodecdec.c
@@ -38,6 +38,10 @@
 #include "decode.h"
 #include "libavutil/dovi_meta.h"
 #include "av1_parse.h"
